{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013KCuHYQZH6PQ1ZfzGXw7Rr","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tslug: pose-review-declared-limits-followups\n3\tstatus: in-progress        # draft | in-progress | done | superseded | abandoned; blocked = operational wait, not terminal\n4\tcreated_at: 2026-11-26\n5\tcompleted_at:        # stamped on the transition to status: done\n6\tsupersedes:          # slug of the superseded spec (when applicable)\n7\tdepends_on:          # prerequisites, inline list: other-spec, milestone:<roadmap>/<id>, roadmap:<slug>\n8\tremediates:          # optional explicit links: spec:slug@defect-fix, finding:rva-<16hex>/F1@revert (never inferred from depends_on)\n9\tpriority: 2\n10\tcomponents: pose-mcp\n11\ttask_type: bugfix\n12\tsurface: standard\n13\tdelivers: capability:review-declared-limits-followups\n14\t---\n15\t\n16\t# Spec: pose-review-declared-limits-followups\n17\t\n18\t## 1. Intent\n19\t\n20\t### Goal\n21\tClose the follow-ups left by `pose-review-declared-threat-model`: the remaining Markdown the accepted-limits reader misreads, a limit named by a non-approving draft, the manual `--finding` path, the published schemas, and the text output of the checks.\n22\t\n23\t### Business value\n24\tThe spec closed on 2026-11-26 after eleven review rounds; its Final Report lists two follow-ups and its approving attestation five more (round 11, N1–N5).\n25\t\n26\t### Constraints\n27\tEach item keeps the behaviour its origin spec delivered; a fix that changes an answer states it as a decision.\n28\t\n29\t### Non-goals\n30\tReopening the decisions of the origin spec.\n31\t\n32\t## 2. Requirements\n33\t\n34\t### Functional\n35\t- R1: An indented continuation line (one to three spaces) that starts with `# ` shall not end the section and cut the limit: it is either read as the limit's text or reported, and the limit is not sealed in part (round 11, N1).\n36\t- R2: An unterminated `<!--` anywhere, also after a closed comment, and any comment marker inside the accepted limits section, inline code included, shall be reported, and no limit shall be sealed cut by them (rounds 9 N4, 10 N4, 11 N2; D1).\n37\t- R3: `pose review attest --finding` shall accept a limit for a `within-limit` finding, or the CLI reference shall stop listing it there (round 11, N3).\n38\t- R4: A non-approving draft whose follow-up names a limit the bundle did not seal shall be refused or recorded without `within-limit`, so no attestation names a limit that does not exist (round 11, N4).\n39\t- R5: The published review plan and bundle schemas shall declare `accepted_limits` (and `limitations`), with the schema drift test covering them (round 11, N5).\n40\t- R6: `pose review-check` and `pose closeout-check` shall show within-limit findings in their text output, as their JSON does (rounds 9 N5, 10 N5).\n41\t\n42\t### Non-functional\n43\tExisting behaviour outside the stated requirements is unchanged.\n44\t\n45\t### Security\n46\tNo new input crosses a trust boundary without the existing confinement.\n47\t\n48\t### Compatibility\n49\tRecords and indexes written by earlier engines keep their meaning.\n50\t\n51\t## 3. Technical Plan\n52\t\n53\t### Affected areas\n54\t`pose-mcp`: `accepted_limits.go`, `review_conclusions.go`, `review_bundle.go`, the attest CLI, the published schemas, `review-check`/`closeout-check` output, `docs-site/docs/cli.md`.\n55\t\n56\t### Artifacts\n57\t- created: .pose/specs/2026-11-26-pose-review-declared-limits-followups.md\n58\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\n59\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits_test.go\n60\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go\n61\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/schema_test.go\n62\t- modified: pose-mcp/schemas/v1/review-plan.schema.json\n63\t- modified: pose-mcp/schemas/v1/review-bundle.schema.json\n64\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n65\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/accepted_limits_lint_test.go\n66\t- modified: docs-site/docs/cli.md\n67\t- modified: POSE.md\n68\t- modified: locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n69\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\n70\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n71\t\n72\t### Delivery targets\n73\t- capability:review-declared-limits-followups module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go\n74\t\n75\t### API/contract changes\n76\t`pose review attest --finding` takes a ninth field, `limit`. The review plan and bundle schemas declare `accepted_limits` and `limitations`. `pose review-check` and `pose closeout-check` print `review.within_limit` / `closeout.within_limit` lines.\n77\t\n78\t### Data/storage changes\n79\tNone.\n80\t\n81\t### Technical risks\n82\tA spec whose accepted limits section held an HTML comment now has its limits refused; none in this repository does.\n83\t\n84\t## 4. Tasks\n85\t\n86\t### Planning\n87\t- [x] Confirm each requirement against the current engine before starting.\n88\t\n89\t### Implementation\n90\t- [x] Implement each requirement with a test that fails before it.\n91\t\n92\t### Validation\n93\t- [ ] `pose validate --carry` and `pose check --strict`.\n94\t\n95\t## 5. Decisions\n96\t\n97\t### Decision D1\n98\t- Basis: R2\n99\tR2 as drafted asked that a comment written in inline code keep its text. Telling inline code from a real comment is the kind of Markdown reading that took the origin spec four rounds to make fail-closed; instead, any comment marker inside the accepted limits section refuses the section whole, and the ready check says so. A comment outside the section, including one that holds an example section, is still stripped and not read. A marker written in inline code (an odd number of backticks before it on its line) opens no comment, as Markdown shows it as text; the spec's own ready check found that its R2, which names the marker, was taken for an unterminated comment.\n100\t\n101\t## 6. Validation\n102\t\n103\t### Strategy\n104\tEach requirement gets a regression test shown failing before its code.\n105\t\n106\t### Deterministic checks\n107\t\n108\t#### Test\n109\t- Command: `go test ./...` (in `pose-mcp`), then `pose validate --carry`.\n110\t\n111\t### Execution log\n112\t- 2026-11-27: R1 reports a heading-like line indented under a limit; R2 reports any unterminated comment and any comment marker in the section (D1); R3 adds `limit` to `--finding`; R4 records `within-limit` only for a sealed limit; R5 declares the fields in both schemas; R6 prints within-limit findings. `TestAcceptedLimitsRefuseWhatWouldCutThem`, `TestOnlyASealedLimitIsRecordedWithinLimit`, `TestSchemaDrift`, `TestTheBundleSchemaDeclaresTheAcceptedLimits` and `TestWithinLimitFindingsAreTypedAndShown` fail with each guard mutated out.\n113\t- 2026-11-27: this spec's own ready check failed: its R2 names `<!--` in inline code, which the new check took for an unterminated comment. A marker in inline code now opens no comment (`htmlCommentStart`, `stripLimitComments`); `TestAcceptedLimitsIgnoreAMarkerNamedInCode` fails with the backtick rule mutated out. The five specs of this repository that declare accepted limits pass the ready check unchanged.\n114\t\n115\t### Results summary\n116\tThe full `pose-mcp` suite passes; the canonical result is refreshed with `pose validate --carry`.\n117\t\n118\t### Requirement trace\n119\t- R1 [satisfied] test:TestAcceptedLimitsRefuseWhatWouldCutThem\n120\t- R2 [satisfied] test:TestAcceptedLimitsRefuseWhatWouldCutThem, test:TestAcceptedLimitsIgnoreAMarkerNamedInCode, test:TestAcceptedLimitsReadWrappedEntriesAndSkipExamples\n121\t- R3 [satisfied] test:TestWithinLimitFindingsAreTypedAndShown\n122\t- R4 [satisfied] test:TestOnlyASealedLimitIsRecordedWithinLimit\n123\t- R5 [satisfied] test:TestSchemaDrift, test:TestTheBundleSchemaDeclaresTheAcceptedLimits\n124\t- R6 [satisfied] test:TestWithinLimitFindingsAreTypedAndShown\n125\t\n126\t### Known gaps\n127\tNone.\n128\t\n129\t## 7. Final Report\n130\t\n131\t### Delivered scope\n132\tThe accepted-limits reader refuses what would cut a limit; a within-limit finding can be typed, names only a sealed limit, is declared in the schemas and shown by the checks.\n133\t\n134\t### Files and modules changed\n135\t`pose-mcp` accepted limits, conclusions, attest CLI, check output and schemas; the CLI reference and the manual in both locales with their embedded copies.\n136\t\n137\t### Validation executed\n138\t`go test ./...` in `pose-mcp`; `pose check --strict`; `pose validate --carry --json-out .pose/results/delivery-validation.json`.\n139\t\n140\t### Residual risks\n141\tNone beyond those of the origin spec.\n142\t\n143\t### Follow-ups\n144\tNone. Origin: `pose-review-declared-threat-model` (done 2026-11-26).\n145\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"a3e30b84-e3da-4ad5-9050-7e08212eeedb","timestamp":"2026-11-27T12:02:17.517Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-f7649a2054/worktree/.pose/specs/2026-11-26-pose-review-declared-limits-followups.md","content":"---\nslug: pose-review-declared-limits-followups\nstatus: in-progress        # draft | in-progress | done | superseded | abandoned; blocked = operational wait, not terminal\ncreated_at: 2026-11-26\ncompleted_at:        # stamped on the transition to status: done\nsupersedes:          # slug of the superseded spec (when applicable)\ndepends_on:          # prerequisites, inline list: other-spec, milestone:<roadmap>/<id>, roadmap:<slug>\nremediates:          # optional explicit links: spec:slug@defect-fix, finding:rva-<16hex>/F1@revert (never inferred from depends_on)\npriority: 2\ncomponents: pose-mcp\ntask_type: bugfix\nsurface: standard\ndelivers: capability:review-declared-limits-followups\n---\n\n# Spec: pose-review-declared-limits-followups\n\n## 1. Intent\n\n### Goal\nClose the follow-ups left by `pose-review-declared-threat-model`: the remaining Markdown the accepted-limits reader misreads, a limit named by a non-approving draft, the manual `--finding` path, the published schemas, and the text output of the checks.\n\n### Business value\nThe spec closed on 2026-11-26 after eleven review rounds; its Final Report lists two follow-ups and its approving attestation five more (round 11, N1–N5).\n\n### Constraints\nEach item keeps the behaviour its origin spec delivered; a fix that changes an answer states it as a decision.\n\n### Non-goals\nReopening the decisions of the origin spec.\n\n## 2. Requirements\n\n### Functional\n- R1: An indented continuation line (one to three spaces) that starts with `# ` shall not end the section and cut the limit: it is either read as the limit's text or reported, and the limit is not sealed in part (round 11, N1).\n- R2: An unterminated `<!--` anywhere, also after a closed comment, and any comment marker inside the accepted limits section, inline code included, shall be reported, and no limit shall be sealed cut by them (rounds 9 N4, 10 N4, 11 N2; D1).\n- R3: `pose review attest --finding` shall accept a limit for a `within-limit` finding, or the CLI reference shall stop listing it there (round 11, N3).\n- R4: A non-approving draft whose follow-up names a limit the bundle did not seal shall be refused or recorded without `within-limit`, so no attestation names a limit that does not exist (round 11, N4).\n- R5: The published review plan and bundle schemas shall declare `accepted_limits` (and `limitations`), with the schema drift test covering them (round 11, N5).\n- R6: `pose review-check` and `pose closeout-check` shall show within-limit findings in their text output, as their JSON does (rounds 9 N5, 10 N5).\n\n### Non-functional\nExisting behaviour outside the stated requirements is unchanged.\n\n### Security\nNo new input crosses a trust boundary without the existing confinement.\n\n### Compatibility\nRecords and indexes written by earlier engines keep their meaning.\n\n## 3. Technical Plan\n\n### Affected areas\n`pose-mcp`: `accepted_limits.go`, `review_conclusions.go`, `review_bundle.go`, the attest CLI, the published schemas, `review-check`/`closeout-check` output, `docs-site/docs/cli.md`.\n\n### Artifacts\n- created: .pose/specs/2026-11-26-pose-review-declared-limits-followups.md\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits_test.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/schema_test.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/schemas/v1/review-plan.schema.json\n- modified: pose-mcp/schemas/v1/review-bundle.schema.json\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/accepted_limits_lint_test.go\n- modified: docs-site/docs/cli.md\n- modified: POSE.md\n- modified: locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n\n### Delivery targets\n- capability:review-declared-limits-followups module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go\n\n### API/contract changes\n`pose review attest --finding` takes a ninth field, `limit`. The review plan and bundle schemas declare `accepted_limits` and `limitations`. `pose review-check` and `pose closeout-check` print `review.within_limit` / `closeout.within_limit` lines.\n\n### Data/storage changes\nNone.\n\n### Technical risks\nA spec whose accepted limits section held an HTML comment now has its limits refused; none in this repository does.\n\n## 4. Tasks\n\n### Planning\n- [x] Confirm each requirement against the current engine before starting.\n\n### Implementation\n- [x] Implement each requirement with a test that fails before it.\n\n### Validation\n- [ ] `pose validate --carry` and `pose check --strict`.\n\n## 5. Decisions\n\n### Decision D1\n- Basis: R2\nR2 as drafted asked that a comment written in inline code keep its text. Telling inline code from a real comment is the kind of Markdown reading that took the origin spec four rounds to make fail-closed; instead, any comment marker inside the accepted limits section refuses the section whole, and the ready check says so. A comment outside the section, including one that holds an example section, is still stripped and not read. A marker written in inline code (an odd number of backticks before it on its line) opens no comment, as Markdown shows it as text; the spec's own ready check found that its R2, which names the marker, was taken for an unterminated comment.\n\n## 6. Validation\n\n### Strategy\nEach requirement gets a regression test shown failing before its code.\n\n### Deterministic checks\n\n#### Test\n- Command: `go test ./...` (in `pose-mcp`), then `pose validate --carry`.\n\n### Execution log\n- 2026-11-27: R1 reports a heading-like line indented under a limit; R2 reports any unterminated comment and any comment marker in the section (D1); R3 adds `limit` to `--finding`; R4 records `within-limit` only for a sealed limit; R5 declares the fields in both schemas; R6 prints within-limit findings. `TestAcceptedLimitsRefuseWhatWouldCutThem`, `TestOnlyASealedLimitIsRecordedWithinLimit`, `TestSchemaDrift`, `TestTheBundleSchemaDeclaresTheAcceptedLimits` and `TestWithinLimitFindingsAreTypedAndShown` fail with each guard mutated out.\n- 2026-11-27: this spec's own ready check failed: its R2 names `<!--` in inline code, which the new check took for an unterminated comment. A marker in inline code now opens no comment (`htmlCommentStart`, `stripLimitComments`); `TestAcceptedLimitsIgnoreAMarkerNamedInCode` fails with the backtick rule mutated out. The five specs of this repository that declare accepted limits pass the ready check unchanged.\n\n### Results summary\nThe full `pose-mcp` suite passes; the canonical result is refreshed with `pose validate --carry`.\n\n### Requirement trace\n- R1 [satisfied] test:TestAcceptedLimitsRefuseWhatWouldCutThem\n- R2 [satisfied] test:TestAcceptedLimitsRefuseWhatWouldCutThem, test:TestAcceptedLimitsIgnoreAMarkerNamedInCode, test:TestAcceptedLimitsReadWrappedEntriesAndSkipExamples\n- R3 [satisfied] test:TestWithinLimitFindingsAreTypedAndShown\n- R4 [satisfied] test:TestOnlyASealedLimitIsRecordedWithinLimit\n- R5 [satisfied] test:TestSchemaDrift, test:TestTheBundleSchemaDeclaresTheAcceptedLimits\n- R6 [satisfied] test:TestWithinLimitFindingsAreTypedAndShown\n\n### Known gaps\nNone.\n\n## 7. Final Report\n\n### Delivered scope\nThe accepted-limits reader refuses what would cut a limit; a within-limit finding can be typed, names only a sealed limit, is declared in the schemas and shown by the checks.\n\n### Files and modules changed\n`pose-mcp` accepted limits, conclusions, attest CLI, check output and schemas; the CLI reference and the manual in both locales with their embedded copies.\n\n### Validation executed\n`go test ./...` in `pose-mcp`; `pose check --strict`; `pose validate --carry --json-out .pose/results/delivery-validation.json`.\n\n### Residual risks\nNone beyond those of the origin spec.\n\n### Follow-ups\nNone. Origin: `pose-review-declared-threat-model` (done 2026-11-26).\n","numLines":145,"startLine":1,"totalLines":145}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013KCuHYQZH6PQ1ZfzGXw7Rr","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
