{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChTRFvo88Y9DmeCELuefk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\nR2 is not met. The ready check reports a spec as ready while sealing silently drops all its limits, and some layouts still seal a cut limit. I confirmed N1–N5 and N7 with temporary probe tests, injected through `go test -overlay` from `$TMPDIR` so the checkout was not changed.\n\n## Defects\n\n| ID | Severity | Location | Defect |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| N1 | high, blocker | `pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go:574` | The ready check strips closed comments (line 454) before parsing. A comment in the section, inline code included, gives `spec.ready=true`, while the sealing reader returns no limits and `accepted_limits.go:210` drops the problem. This contradicts R2, and D1's \"the ready check says so\". |\n| N2 | high, blocker | `pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:308` | A comment before, after or spanning the section heading makes the detector miss the section. A cut limit is then returned with no problem. With an unterminated comment, a problem is returned but so is the cut limit. |\n| N3 | medium, blocker | `accepted_limits.go:316` | After an indented heading under L1, the detector leaves the section but the parser does not. L2 holding a comment is returned cut. |\n| N4 | medium, blocker | `accepted_limits.go:294` | The detector ignores code fences and a second comment on a line. Examples outside the real section can make it refuse that section, against D1. |\n| N5 | low, follow-up | `accepted_limits.go:114` | If the limit marker is itself indented, a heading-like line not indented deeper still cuts the limit silently. |\n| N6 | low, follow-up | `accepted_limits.go:246` | An unterminated comment after a stray backtick goes unreported. A marker in a double-backtick span is falsely reported. |\n| N7 | low, follow-up | `pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go:1293` | A manual non-approving attestation can store an unsealed limit, such as `L9`. |\n| N8 | low, follow-up | `pose-mcp/internal/cli/accepted_limits_lint_test.go:105` | The R6 test calls the helper directly, so removing either call site would not fail it. This is from reading the code; I did not run that mutation. |\n| N9 | low, follow-up | `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go:188` | Older non-approving attestations naming an unsealed limit would now differ from their recomputed draft. This is inferred from the code; I demonstrated no affected record. |\n\n## Checks\n\n- **Tests:** the focused accepted-limit, schema and ready-check tests pass, and `go vet` on `internal/cli` and `internal/pose` is clean.\n- **Existing specs:** the five specs that declare limits parse with the new reader with no problems. I did not compare their limit text against the old reader.\n- **Not rerun:** I did not run the full `validate` or the `pose-mcp` module `validate`, so both are marked `deferred`. The sealed results are the only evidence for them.\n- **Draft and cleanup:** `review draft-check` accepts the draft below. `go clean -cache` and the `go-build*` removal exited 0.\n\nThe criteria dispositions and their evidence are in the block.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\"schema\":\"pose.review.draft/v1\",\"decision\":\"changes-requested\",\n\"findings\":[\n{\"id\":\"N1\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go\",\"line\":574,\"summary\":\"R2/D1 unmet: the ready check parses text whose terminated HTML comments were already removed (line 454), so a comment in the accepted limits section, inline code included, passes with spec.ready=true while the sealing reader refuses the whole section; accepted_limits.go:210 drops the problems, so the bundle seals no limit and nothing says so.\"},\n{\"id\":\"N2\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\",\"line\":308,\"summary\":\"R2 bypass: a comment on or before the section heading line (trailing, leading or multi-line) makes commentInAcceptedLimitsSection skip the heading, so comments in the section go undetected, are stripped, and a cut limit is sealed with no problem; with an unterminated one the problem is returned but the cut limit is still returned and sealed.\"},\n{\"id\":\"N3\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\",\"line\":316,\"summary\":\"R2 bypass: the comment detector treats a heading indented under a limit as ending the section (the parser does not, since R1), so a later limit L2 holding a comment is returned for sealing cut.\"},\n{\"id\":\"N4\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\",\"line\":294,\"summary\":\"D1 violated: the detector ignores code fences and tracks only the first comment of a line, so a fenced example section outside the real one (with a comment in or after it), or a commented example opened after another comment on the same line, refuses the real section and discards its limits.\"},\n{\"id\":\"N5\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\",\"line\":114,\"summary\":\"R1 is partial: when the limit marker is itself indented, a heading-like line indented one to three spaces but not deeper than the marker still ends the section, and the limit is sealed cut with no problem.\"},\n{\"id\":\"N6\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\",\"line\":246,\"summary\":\"The backtick parity rule misreads Markdown: an unterminated comment after a stray backtick is no longer reported (the earlier first-comment check reported it), and a marker in a double-backtick code span is reported as an unterminated comment.\"},\n{\"id\":\"N7\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\",\"line\":1293,\"summary\":\"The new ninth --finding field is stored for any disposition, and a non-approving manual attestation skips the sealed-limit check (review_bundle.go:3167), so it can record an unsealed limit such as L9; R4 closes only the draft path.\"},\n{\"id\":\"N8\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/accepted_limits_lint_test.go\",\"line\":105,\"summary\":\"The R6 test calls renderWithinLimitFindings directly; removing its calls at review_closeout.go:104 and :328 would not fail it, so the review-check and closeout-check output is untested.\"},\n{\"id\":\"N9\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go\",\"line\":188,\"summary\":\"The changed derivation also applies when runConclusionDiffers recomputes older records: a run-backed non-approving attestation an earlier engine recorded within an unsealed limit would now differ from its draft. No affected record was demonstrated in this repository.\"}\n],\n\"criteria\":[\n{\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-concurrency\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The changed code is pure string reading and rendering with no shared state, goroutines or lifecycle change.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-contracts\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-approval-domain-preflight-integration\",\"rationale\":\"The ninth finding field is optional and the schema additions are optional properties; the focused schema tests pass.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-input-errors\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N2\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-integration-impact\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-observability\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},\n{\"id\":\"compatibility\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N9\"},\n{\"id\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N3\"},\n{\"id\":\"cross-component-integration\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},\n{\"id\":\"design-causality\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N2\"},\n{\"id\":\"documentation\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},\n{\"id\":\"operability\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N4\"},\n{\"id\":\"requirements\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},\n{\"id\":\"scope\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Compared the diff of the implementation files with R1-R6 and the Artifacts list: parser, draft conclusion, attest CLI, check output, two schemas, tests and docs; nothing outside the spec's follow-ups was found in those files.\"},\n{\"id\":\"security\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N2\"},\n{\"id\":\"solution-proportionality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Refusing the section on any comment (D1) is a smaller choice than interpreting Markdown and adds no speculative extension. It depends on one reading of where the section is; the second scanner added for it diverges from the parser (N2-N4), which is the condition that invalidates the choice as implemented.\"}\n],\n\"tools\":[\n{\"id\":\"artifact-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-review-declared-limits-followups --strict\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0; warnings only observed in the inspected output.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-design\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-c230236f14aa5ff3\",\"rationale\":\"Observed, with no structural deltas.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-discover\",\"component\":\"docs-site\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess discover --no-persist --component docs-site\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-discover\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-integrate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Run; three medium gaps about unobserved HTTP consumers, none on the changed surfaces.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-tech-debt\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\"rationale\":\"Run; the scan reports itself incomplete for two unreadable specs outside this change.\"},\n{\"id\":\"closeout-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Post-review gate; run now, it reports the spec not done and no approved review.\"},\n{\"id\":\"review-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Post-review gate; run now, it reports no current review record.\"},\n{\"id\":\"suggest-review\",\"component\":\"docs-site\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose suggest review --path docs-site\"},\n{\"id\":\"suggest-review\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\"},\n{\"id\":\"surface-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Run with --strict: zero findings.\"},\n{\"id\":\"validate\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"The full validate was not rerun in this run, to stay within its time and cache limits; the sealed results are the only evidence for it.\"},\n{\"id\":\"validate\",\"component\":\"docs-site\",\"disposition\":\"not-used\",\"rationale\":\"Run: the validation matrix matched no check for docs-site (0 steps), so nothing can emit the evidence classes.\"},\n{\"id\":\"validate\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"The full module validate was not rerun in this run; only the focused accepted-limit and schema tests and go vet on internal/cli and internal/pose were run, and they pass. The sealed results cover the rest.\"}\n]}\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":362,"cache_read_input_tokens":124901,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":362},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"3d088f0f-2cee-4ad2-8abe-8e1946bdaabb","timestamp":"2026-11-27T12:18:16.737Z","request_id":"req_011ChTRFvbTQLpHhd4YTdBYj"}
{"duration_api_ms":200245,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"[private-session]","total_cost_usd":0.9112305,"usage":{"input_tokens":34,"cache_creation_input_tokens":119117,"cache_read_input_tokens":1394245,"output_tokens":29527,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":12209},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":119117,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4165,"cache_read_input_tokens":124901,"cache_creation_input_tokens":362,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":362},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"inputTokens":34,"outputTokens":29527,"cacheReadInputTokens":1394245,"cacheCreationInputTokens":119117,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.9112305,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":12209,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":119117,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":43,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"decision: changes-requested\n\nR2 is not met. The ready check reports a spec as ready while sealing silently drops all its limits, and some layouts still seal a cut limit. I confirmed N1–N5 and N7 with temporary probe tests, injected through `go test -overlay` from `$TMPDIR` so the checkout was not changed.\n\n## Defects\n\n| ID | Severity | Location | Defect |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| N1 | high, blocker | `pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go:574` | The ready check strips closed comments (line 454) before parsing. A comment in the section, inline code included, gives `spec.ready=true`, while the sealing reader returns no limits and `accepted_limits.go:210` drops the problem. This contradicts R2, and D1's \"the ready check says so\". |\n| N2 | high, blocker | `pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:308` | A comment before, after or spanning the section heading makes the detector miss the section. A cut limit is then returned with no problem. With an unterminated comment, a problem is returned but so is the cut limit. |\n| N3 | medium, blocker | `accepted_limits.go:316` | After an indented heading under L1, the detector leaves the section but the parser does not. L2 holding a comment is returned cut. |\n| N4 | medium, blocker | `accepted_limits.go:294` | The detector ignores code fences and a second comment on a line. Examples outside the real section can make it refuse that section, against D1. |\n| N5 | low, follow-up | `accepted_limits.go:114` | If the limit marker is itself indented, a heading-like line not indented deeper still cuts the limit silently. |\n| N6 | low, follow-up | `accepted_limits.go:246` | An unterminated comment after a stray backtick goes unreported. A marker in a double-backtick span is falsely reported. |\n| N7 | low, follow-up | `pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go:1293` | A manual non-approving attestation can store an unsealed limit, such as `L9`. |\n| N8 | low, follow-up | `pose-mcp/internal/cli/accepted_limits_lint_test.go:105` | The R6 test calls the helper directly, so removing either call site would not fail it. This is from reading the code; I did not run that mutation. |\n| N9 | low, follow-up | `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go:188` | Older non-approving attestations naming an unsealed limit would now differ from their recomputed draft. This is inferred from the code; I demonstrated no affected record. |\n\n## Checks\n\n- **Tests:** the focused accepted-limit, schema and ready-check tests pass, and `go vet` on `internal/cli` and `internal/pose` is clean.\n- **Existing specs:** the five specs that declare limits parse with the new reader with no problems. I did not compare their limit text against the old reader.\n- **Not rerun:** I did not run the full `validate` or the `pose-mcp` module `validate`, so both are marked `deferred`. The sealed results are the only evidence for them.\n- **Draft and cleanup:** `review draft-check` accepts the draft below. `go clean -cache` and the `go-build*` removal exited 0.\n\nThe criteria dispositions and their evidence are in the block.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\"schema\":\"pose.review.draft/v1\",\"decision\":\"changes-requested\",\n\"findings\":[\n{\"id\":\"N1\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go\",\"line\":574,\"summary\":\"R2/D1 unmet: the ready check parses text whose terminated HTML comments were already removed (line 454), so a comment in the accepted limits section, inline code included, passes with spec.ready=true while the sealing reader refuses the whole section; accepted_limits.go:210 drops the problems, so the bundle seals no limit and nothing says so.\"},\n{\"id\":\"N2\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\",\"line\":308,\"summary\":\"R2 bypass: a comment on or before the section heading line (trailing, leading or multi-line) makes commentInAcceptedLimitsSection skip the heading, so comments in the section go undetected, are stripped, and a cut limit is sealed with no problem; with an unterminated one the problem is returned but the cut limit is still returned and sealed.\"},\n{\"id\":\"N3\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\",\"line\":316,\"summary\":\"R2 bypass: the comment detector treats a heading indented under a limit as ending the section (the parser does not, since R1), so a later limit L2 holding a comment is returned for sealing cut.\"},\n{\"id\":\"N4\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\",\"line\":294,\"summary\":\"D1 violated: the detector ignores code fences and tracks only the first comment of a line, so a fenced example section outside the real one (with a comment in or after it), or a commented example opened after another comment on the same line, refuses the real section and discards its limits.\"},\n{\"id\":\"N5\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\",\"line\":114,\"summary\":\"R1 is partial: when the limit marker is itself indented, a heading-like line indented one to three spaces but not deeper than the marker still ends the section, and the limit is sealed cut with no problem.\"},\n{\"id\":\"N6\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\",\"line\":246,\"summary\":\"The backtick parity rule misreads Markdown: an unterminated comment after a stray backtick is no longer reported (the earlier first-comment check reported it), and a marker in a double-backtick code span is reported as an unterminated comment.\"},\n{\"id\":\"N7\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\",\"line\":1293,\"summary\":\"The new ninth --finding field is stored for any disposition, and a non-approving manual attestation skips the sealed-limit check (review_bundle.go:3167), so it can record an unsealed limit such as L9; R4 closes only the draft path.\"},\n{\"id\":\"N8\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/accepted_limits_lint_test.go\",\"line\":105,\"summary\":\"The R6 test calls renderWithinLimitFindings directly; removing its calls at review_closeout.go:104 and :328 would not fail it, so the review-check and closeout-check output is untested.\"},\n{\"id\":\"N9\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go\",\"line\":188,\"summary\":\"The changed derivation also applies when runConclusionDiffers recomputes older records: a run-backed non-approving attestation an earlier engine recorded within an unsealed limit would now differ from its draft. No affected record was demonstrated in this repository.\"}\n],\n\"criteria\":[\n{\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-concurrency\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The changed code is pure string reading and rendering with no shared state, goroutines or lifecycle change.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-contracts\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-approval-domain-preflight-integration\",\"rationale\":\"The ninth finding field is optional and the schema additions are optional properties; the focused schema tests pass.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-input-errors\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N2\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-integration-impact\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-observability\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},\n{\"id\":\"compatibility\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N9\"},\n{\"id\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N3\"},\n{\"id\":\"cross-component-integration\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},\n{\"id\":\"design-causality\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N2\"},\n{\"id\":\"documentation\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},\n{\"id\":\"operability\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N4\"},\n{\"id\":\"requirements\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},\n{\"id\":\"scope\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Compared the diff of the implementation files with R1-R6 and the Artifacts list: parser, draft conclusion, attest CLI, check output, two schemas, tests and docs; nothing outside the spec's follow-ups was found in those files.\"},\n{\"id\":\"security\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N2\"},\n{\"id\":\"solution-proportionality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Refusing the section on any comment (D1) is a smaller choice than interpreting Markdown and adds no speculative extension. It depends on one reading of where the section is; the second scanner added for it diverges from the parser (N2-N4), which is the condition that invalidates the choice as implemented.\"}\n],\n\"tools\":[\n{\"id\":\"artifact-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-review-declared-limits-followups --strict\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0; warnings only observed in the inspected output.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-design\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-c230236f14aa5ff3\",\"rationale\":\"Observed, with no structural deltas.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-discover\",\"component\":\"docs-site\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess discover --no-persist --component docs-site\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-discover\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-integrate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Run; three medium gaps about unobserved HTTP consumers, none on the changed surfaces.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-tech-debt\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\"rationale\":\"Run; the scan reports itself incomplete for two unreadable specs outside this change.\"},\n{\"id\":\"closeout-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Post-review gate; run now, it reports the spec not done and no approved review.\"},\n{\"id\":\"review-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Post-review gate; run now, it reports no current review record.\"},\n{\"id\":\"suggest-review\",\"component\":\"docs-site\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose suggest review --path docs-site\"},\n{\"id\":\"suggest-review\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\"},\n{\"id\":\"surface-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Run with --strict: zero findings.\"},\n{\"id\":\"validate\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"The full validate was not rerun in this run, to stay within its time and cache limits; the sealed results are the only evidence for it.\"},\n{\"id\":\"validate\",\"component\":\"docs-site\",\"disposition\":\"not-used\",\"rationale\":\"Run: the validation matrix matched no check for docs-site (0 steps), so nothing can emit the evidence classes.\"},\n{\"id\":\"validate\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"The full module validate was not rerun in this run; only the focused accepted-limit and schema tests and go vet on internal/cli and internal/pose were run, and they pass. The sealed results cover the rest.\"}\n]}\n```","ttft_ms":907,"type":"result","duration_ms":963214,"uuid":"fcbc6dc8-ae51-4383-b77e-8179851b4ee2","ttft_stream_ms":650,"time_to_request_ms":51,"first_content_frame_ms":650,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"inputTokens":34,"outputTokens":29527,"cacheReadInputTokens":1394245,"cacheCreationInputTokens":119117,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.9112305,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thi